  "status_text": "One penalty can stand in for every way you might charge two lights. Lean checked when this happens (L-lib-1372). Take two patterns of lit bulbs. If the price for those lit in both plus the price for those lit in either exceeds the two original prices added together, the charge can reproduce any two-light price. Fix the other lights, weight the original charge, and add single-light and directed on-to-off charges. The result matches the chosen price up to a scale and a baseline. The same circuit provides both lights, with existing constants for the rest.",
